From 315035fdef35b20f2833775b814b31fac983c261 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:17:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run 7: the tag search counts in the same statement, not a
 second one

search_contacts ran its count as a second statement that repeated the whole
matched-labels work and held a second long-pool connection. In run 7 (200 at
once) this search was 732 of the 1,203 slow lines, waiting a median 10.9 s
for a connection against 2.1 s in the database. The count is now a scalar
subquery over the same CTE in the same statement: the match runs once, on
one connection. Same rows, same total.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
